## Free vs. Open Source: An Important Distinction

People often conflate "free" (no cost) with "open source." They are different:

| | Free (Freeware) | Open Source |
|---|---|---|
| Cost | $0 | Usually $0 |
| Code visible? | ❌ No | ✅ Yes |
| Can modify? | ❌ No | ✅ Yes |
| Can redistribute? | ❌ No | ✅ Yes |
| Verified no tracking? | ❌ No | ✅ Verifiable |
| Community contributions | ❌ No | ✅ Yes |

A "free" app with closed source code can:
- Show ads (and keep all revenue)
- Collect data and sell it to data brokers
- Change its business model at any time
- Disappear from the Play Store with no recourse

An open source app, even if its Play Store version disappears, has its code preserved. The community can fork it, maintain it, and redistribute it.

