## Community Contributions: How Open Source Improves Over Time

When source code is public, anyone who uses the app can become a contributor:

- A user notices a bug → opens an issue on GitHub → the developer (or another community member) fixes it
- A developer in another country needs the app in their language → submits a translation pull request
- A user with a specific TV model (e.g., a Hisense model with quirky behavior) → submits a bug fix for that model
- A security researcher finds a potential vulnerability → responsibly discloses it on GitHub → it gets patched quickly

This crowdsourced improvement model is one of the key reasons open source software tends to be higher quality than closed-source alternatives over time. Problems are discovered and fixed faster. Features that matter to users get added.

